---
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { withBase } from "../../utils/url";
const capabilities = [
  ["Public communication", "Institutional pages, news, recruitment information, history, contacts and an organised document area."],
  ["Protected member services", "A personal login environment for communications, forms, accreditation requests, profile management and editorial proposals."],
  ["Role-based administration", "Dedicated tools for accreditation management, response analysis, news review and account administration according to assigned permissions."],
  ["Installable experience", "A Progressive Web App based on the same member area, distributed through the browser and updated through the WordPress service worker."],
];
---
<BaseLayout title="AIA Udine Web Platform | Riccardo Paravano" description="Case study of the AIA Udine institutional website and protected member-service platform.">
  <article class="container page case-study">
    <a class="back" href={withBase("/projects/")}>â† All projects</a>
    <header class="case-header"><div><p class="eyebrow">Web platform and digital services</p><h1>AIA Udine Web Platform</h1><p class="lead">I designed, developed and now maintain the official digital platform of the AIA Udine section, combining a public institutional website with protected services for members, managers and administrators.</p></div><aside><span>Role</span><strong>Web developer & webmaster</strong><span>Stack</span><strong>WordPress, PHP, MySQL, JavaScript</strong><span>Status</span><strong>Live and evolving</strong></aside></header>
    <section><p class="eyebrow">The challenge</p><h2>One platform for communication and section operations.</h2><p>The project had to serve two different contexts without fragmenting the experience: public communication for prospective referees and the local community, and authenticated operational services for association members. The solution needed to remain clear on mobile, manageable by authorised staff and extensible as new workflows were introduced.</p></section>
    <section><p class="eyebrow">What I delivered</p><div class="capability-grid">{capabilities.map((item) => <div class="capability"><h3>{item[0]}</h3><p>{item[1]}</p></div>)}</div></section>
    <section class="split"><div><p class="eyebrow">My contribution</p><h2>Ownership beyond the initial build.</h2></div><div><p>I worked across information architecture, interface design, WordPress customisation, plugin integration and custom functionality. I also manage updates, performance, compatibility and the evolution of communication workflows. This makes the project a product-maintenance responsibility, not a one-off website delivery.</p><p>The current platform exposes public documents, news and recruitment content, while the protected area centralises communications, forms and accreditation workflows. The installable PWA reuses the same platform and receives updates automatically.</p></div></section>
    <section class="outcome"><p class="eyebrow">Outcome</p><h2>A clearer public presence and a controlled service layer for members.</h2><p>The resulting platform provides a single institutional entry point, responsive access from desktop and smartphone, differentiated permissions for operational roles and an extensible base for future documents, historical content, photographs and services.</p><a class="button button--primary" href="https://www.aiaudine.com/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Visit the live website</a></section>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
.case-study{max-width:1120px}.back{display:inline-block;margin-bottom:3rem;color:var(--muted);font-weight:750}.case-header{display:grid;grid-template-columns:minmax(0,1.45fr) minmax(16rem,.55fr);gap:clamp(2rem,7vw,6rem);align-items:end;padding-bottom:5rem}.case-header aside{display:grid;gap:.35rem;padding:1.5rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:1rem;background:var(--surface)}.case-header aside span{margin-top:.8rem;color:var(--muted);font-size:.78rem}.case-header aside span:first-child{margin-top:0}.case-study section{padding:4.5rem 0;border-top:1px solid var(--border)}.case-study section>p:not(.eyebrow),.split div:last-child p,.outcome p{max-width:75ch;color:var(--muted);font-size:1.05rem}.capability-grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:1rem}.capability{padding:1.5rem;border:1px solid var(--border);border-radius:1rem;background:var(--surface)}.capability p{margin-bottom:0;color:var(--muted)}.split{display:grid;grid-template-columns:.8fr 1.2fr;gap:clamp(2rem,7vw,6rem)}.outcome{padding:clamp(2rem,5vw,4rem)!important;border:1px solid var(--border)!important;border-radius:1.4rem;background:linear-gradient(135deg,rgba(142,197,244,.1),var(--surface))}.outcome .button{margin-top:1rem}@media(max-width:800px){.case-header,.split,.capability-grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.case-header{padding-bottom:3rem}}
</style>